  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $\u03a6(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X\u223cN(-1,{\\sigma }^{2})$ and $P(X>1)=0.0618,$ use the table to find $\\sigma ,$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.4\\,$ | $\\,0.9251\\,$ | $\\,0.9265\\,$ | $\\,0.9279\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.5\\,$ | $\\,0.9382\\,$ | $\\,0.9394\\,$ | $\\,0.9406\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.6\\,$ | $\\,0.9495\\,$ | $\\,0.9505\\,$ | $\\,0.9515\\,$ |\n\n$\\sigma \u2248$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "First, we convert the given probability into a cumulative probability using the complement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 1) & =1-P(X>1) \\\\  & =1-0.0618 \\\\  & =0.9382\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 1) & =0.9382 \\\\ P\\,(Z\\le \\frac{1-(-1)}{\\sigma }) & =0.9382 \\\\ \u03a6\\,(\\frac{2}{\\sigma }) & =0.9382 \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sigma } & ={\u03a6}^{-1}(0.9382)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\n\u03a6(1.54)=0.9382\\,\u21d2\\,{\u03a6}^{-1}(0.9382)=1.54.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sigma } & =1.54 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{2}{1.54} \\\\ \\sigma  & \u22481.30,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places.",
